1. Why is Lazy Evaluation important in Stream API?
==============================================================================

Answer:
Intermediate operations do not execute until a terminal operation is called.

Input:
[5, 15, 25]

Code Without Terminal Operation:

Stream<Integer> stream =
    List.of(5,15,25)
        .stream()
        .filter(n -> {
            System.out.println("Checking: " + n);
            return n > 10;
        });

Output:
No Output

Reason:
filter() is lazy, and no terminal operation has been called.


Code With Terminal Operation:

List<Integer> result =
    List.of(5,15,25)
        .stream()
        .filter(n -> {
            System.out.println("Checking: " + n);
            return n > 10;
        })
        .toList();

System.out.println(result);

Output:
Checking: 5
Checking: 15
Checking: 25
[15, 25]

Interview Point:
Lazy evaluation avoids unnecessary processing and enables
short-circuiting and operation fusion.

Memory Trick:
Lazy = Execute Later

