2. What is Stream Fusion?
==============================================================================

Answer:
Stream Fusion combines multiple intermediate operations into a
single element-by-element traversal.

Input:
[5, 15, 25]

Code:

List<Integer> result =
    List.of(5,15,25)
        .stream()
        .filter(n -> n > 10)
        .map(n -> n * 2)
        .toList();

System.out.println(result);

Output:
[30, 50]

Internal Processing:

5  -> filter fails

15 -> filter passes -> map to 30

25 -> filter passes -> map to 50

Important:
The Stream does not normally create one temporary List after filter()
and another temporary List after map().

Interview Point:
Stream Fusion reduces unnecessary intermediate storage by passing
each element through the connected pipeline stages.

Memory Trick:
Fusion = One Pass

