3. Why should Primitive Streams be used for numerical processing?
==============================================================================

Answer:
Primitive Streams work directly with primitive values and avoid
repeated boxing and unboxing.

Input:
[10, 20, 30]

Code:

int sum =
    List.of(10,20,30)
        .stream()
        .mapToInt(Integer::intValue)
        .sum();

System.out.println(sum);

Output:
60

Primitive Stream Types:

IntStream
LongStream
DoubleStream

Interview Point:
Use IntStream, LongStream, or DoubleStream for large numerical
calculations to reduce wrapper-object overhead.

Memory Trick:
Primitive Stream = No Wrapper Objects

