4. What is Boxing and Unboxing overhead?
==============================================================================

Answer:

Boxing:
int -> Integer

Unboxing:
Integer -> int

Input:
[10, 20, 30]

Code Using Wrapper Stream:

int sum =
    Stream.of(10,20,30)
          .reduce(0, Integer::sum);

System.out.println(sum);

Output:
60


Code Using Primitive Stream:

int sum =
    IntStream.of(10,20,30)
             .sum();

System.out.println(sum);

Output:
60

Difference:

Stream<Integer>
---------------
Works with Integer wrapper objects.

IntStream
---------
Works directly with int values.

Interview Point:
For high-volume numeric processing, primitive Streams can reduce
boxing, unboxing, memory allocation, and garbage-collection pressure.

