8. How should an efficient Stream Pipeline be designed?
==============================================================================

Answer:
Apply inexpensive and highly selective filters before costly
operations such as sorting or complex mapping.

Input:
[40, 10, 30, 5, 20]

Better Pipeline:

List<Integer> result =
    List.of(40,10,30,5,20)
        .stream()
        .filter(n -> n >= 20)
        .sorted()
        .map(n -> n * 10)
        .toList();

System.out.println(result);

Output:
[200, 300, 400]

Flow:

Input:
[40, 10, 30, 5, 20]

After filter:
[40, 30, 20]

After sorted:
[20, 30, 40]

After map:
[200, 300, 400]

Interview Point:
Filter early, minimize data before stateful operations, avoid
unnecessary pipeline stages, and keep lambdas stateless.

Memory Trick:

Filter
  ->
Transform
  ->
Sort if required
  ->
Collect

