12. When would you create a Custom Spliterator?
==============================================================================

Answer:
Create a Custom Spliterator for a custom data source or when special
traversal and splitting behavior is required.

Input:
[10, 20, 30]

Code:

Spliterator<Integer> spliterator =
    List.of(10,20,30)
        .spliterator();

spliterator.tryAdvance(System.out::println);

spliterator.forEachRemaining(System.out::println);

Output:
10
20
30

Explanation:

tryAdvance()
------------
Processes one element.

forEachRemaining()
------------------
Processes all remaining elements.

Custom Spliterator Declaration:

class MySpliterator
        implements Spliterator<Integer> {

    // Implement:
    // tryAdvance()
    // trySplit()
    // estimateSize()
    // characteristics()
}

Interview Point:
A Custom Spliterator is an advanced choice for specialized traversal,
large custom sources, or improved parallel decomposition.

Memory Trick:
Spliterator = Split + Iterator

